            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Janelle Hill"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a pretty good recipe of Pinakbet. I was always so fond of this dish growing up, being that it was always available at family parties and my grandma's was hands down, the best! Some changes I made: I sauteed the onion, garlic, and tomatoes with patis(fish sauce) then added the pork. I added 1 cup of water with 1 tbs of bagoong alamang(no shrimp or prawns). I used butternut squash, because bitter melon is just not for me or my family. And I added zuchinni cubes. Brought everything to a medium boil for 15mins. But these are just my preferences, thanks for sharing :)",
            "datePublished": "2016-01-11T15:40:35.490Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
